This is mapping the single-byte ISO-IR graphic character sets to TRON code.
(The Extended TRON plane number is not assigned yet.)

For 94-sets, the low byte is in range 0x21 to 0x7E which is the character
code within that set.

For 96-sets, you must add 0x60 (or subtract 0x20) to the character code, to
make it in the range 0x80 to 0xDF.

For most character sets, the high byte of the character code within this
plane will be the same as the final byte of the ISO 2022 escape sequence,
but some have a second intermediate byte which is 0x21; in these cases,
add 0x40 to the final byte value to make the value in range 0x80 to 0xBE.
